e measure of angle \\(A\\), we need to analyze the given figure and use the information provided by the angles around it.\n\n1. **Identify the angles around point \\(A\\)**:\n   The angles around point \\(A\\) are given as \\(100^\\circ\\), \\(110^\\circ\\), and \\(40^\\circ\\). These angles are the exterior angles to the interior angles of the polygon at point \\(A\\).\n\n2. **Understand the relationship between interior and exterior angles**:\n   The exterior angle of a polygon at a vertex is supplementary to the interior angle at that vertex. This means that the sum of an interior angle and its corresponding exterior angle is \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the interior angles corresponding to the given exterior angles**:\n   - The exterior angle of \\(100^\\circ\\) corresponds to an interior angle of \\(180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\\).\n   - The exterior angle of \\(110^\\circ\\) corresponds to an interior angle of \\(180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ\\).\n   - The exterior angle of \\(40^\\circ\\) corresponds to an interior angle of \\(180^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 140^\\circ\\).\n\n4. **Sum the interior angles around point \\(A\\)**:\n   The sum of the interior angles around point \\(A\\) is the sum of these three interior angles:\n   \\[\n   80^\\circ + 70^\\circ + 140^\\circ = 290^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determine the measure of angle \\(A\\)**:\n   Since the sum of the interior angles around point \\(A\\) is \\(290^\\circ\\), the measure of angle \\(A\\) must be the remaining angle to make a full circle (which is \\(360^\\circ\\)):\n   \\[\n   360^\\circ - 290^\\circ = 70^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the interior degree measure of angle \\(A\\) is \\(\\boxed{70}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{70}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
